WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.126
Understanding South Africa's

00:00:01.126 --> 00:00:03.461
Genocide Case Against Israel Part Four:

00:00:03.461 --> 00:00:04.963
How the World is Reacting.

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:06.381
Many countries have openly supported

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:08.008
South Africa's case against Israel,

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.676
including the 57 countries

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.720
of the Organization of Islamic Cooperation,

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.179
who issued a statement of support

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.222
and accused Israel of

00:00:14.222 --> 00:00:16.433
“indiscriminate targeting” of civilians.

00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:16.975
Other countries

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:17.934
that have publicly supported

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:18.893
the case are

00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:20.729
Bolivia, Malaysia, Pakistan,

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:22.731
Namibia, Nicaragua, Venezuela.

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:23.773
Meanwhile, the West

00:00:23.773 --> 00:00:24.649
has been pretty united

00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:26.484
in condemning South Africa for this.

00:00:26.484 --> 00:00:28.028
The United States, Israel's oldest

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:30.280
ally, called the case unproductive

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.198
and the genocide allegations unfounded.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.783
Canada, Germany and the U.K.

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:34.367
all insisted

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.326
that Israel has the right

00:00:35.326 --> 00:00:36.411
to defend itself

00:00:36.411 --> 00:00:38.288
and rejected the genocide claims.

00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:39.372
The French foreign minister

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:39.914
said that

00:00:39.914 --> 00:00:41.750
accusing Israel of genocide,

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.293
“cross[es] a moral threshold.”

00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:44.044
Ultimately, it's

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:46.171
this international court’s job to decide

00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:47.964
if South Africa's claims have any merit.

00:00:47.964 --> 00:00:49.424
But remember that the court doesn't

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:50.842
have any way of enforcing it.

00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:51.384
In part five,

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.511
I'll explain what's next for this case.

